# Octo — Rust development

- **Crate:** `octo` — single binary application (Rust 2021). Entry point: `src/main.rs`.
- **Complexity:** treat as a **simple single-crate** project. Prefer `.cursor/rules/rust/simple/single-crate.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/rust/core/code-quality.mdc` unless the user expands scope (workspace, web API, CLI framework, etc.).
- **Rule set:** follow `.cursor/rules/rust/main.mdc` for feature detection and linked rules from [cursor-rust-rules](https://github.com/tyrchen/cursor-rust-rules).
- **Before finishing Rust changes:** run `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` (when clippy is available), and `cargo test`.
- **Errors:** prefer `Result` and `?`; avoid `unwrap()` / `expect()` outside tests or documented invariants.
- **Commit:** `Cargo.lock` stays tracked (application crate).
